# Known divergences (by design): the typmod cross-product table is generated by
# tm.insert_all(), whose dynamic EXECUTE the gateway rejects. It is re-seeded
# (into schema tm) before every test so the ~26k-row table is produced instead of
# cascading into "function does not exist". Because the seed pre-creates schema
# tm, the test's own CREATE SCHEMA tm reports "already exists" -- a one-line
# artifact of the seeding, the honest cost of collapsing the cascade.
